    "question": "A car of mass $1500\\text{ kg}$ traveling on a level road at $10\\text{ m/s}$ brakes to a complete stop. If the braking friction coefficient between tires and road is $\\mu = 0.25$ ($g = 10\\text{ m/s}^2$), the stopping distance of the car calculated using the Work-Energy Theorem is:",
